<title>USA: SmithKline says Sweden clears heart drug.</title>
<headline>SmithKline says Sweden clears heart drug.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swedish Medical Products Agency cleared carvedilol as therapy for congestive heart failure, SmithKline Beecham Plc and Boehringer Mannheim said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Applications for the drug's use in the heart-failure indication are pending in the United States and other countries, the companies said. It gained clearance for that indication in Spain last month.</p>
<p>In the United States, where carvedilol has the brand name Coreg, the drug is being jointly developed by SmithKline Beecham and Boehringer Mannheim, Therapeutics Division.</p>
</text>
